      "id": "j401-h2-mcp",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "source": "## 6. MCP Server — AI Agent Integration\n\nArima exposes a **Model Context Protocol (MCP) server** at `/api/mcp/sse` so AI agents\n(like Claude Desktop) can use Arima as a tool.\n\n### Setup in Claude Desktop (`claude_desktop_config.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"barista-notebooks\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-http\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"SERVER_URL\": \"http://localhost:8585/api/mcp/sse\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nOr use a direct HTTP MCP client pointing to `http://localhost:8585/api/mcp/sse`.\n\n### Available MCP Tools:\n\n| Tool | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `barista_execute_code` | Run Java/JShell code, get output back |\n| `barista_list_notebooks` | List all notebooks |\n| `barista_read_notebook` | Read all cells from a notebook |\n| `barista_run_pipeline` | Execute a pipeline cell |\n| `barista_search_cells` | Search cells by anchor or content |\n| `barista_load_module` | Load a named module into a session |\n\n### Example agent conversation:\n> **Agent:** \"Analyze the spending data in java-401 and tell me the top expense category\"\n> **Agent calls:** `barista_run_pipeline(notebookId=\"java-401\", cellId=\"j401-etl-pipeline\")`\n> **Arima returns:** The full pipeline output\n> **Agent:** \"The top category is Shopping ($130.00)\"\n",
      "output": "",
      "returnValue": null,
      "executed": false,
      "executionCount": null,
      "error": "",
      "anchor": null,
      "dependsOn": [],
      "pipelineSteps": []
